# Inbox -> Assets -> Content JSON -> Build Pipeline

- Source materials live in `inbox/<project-slug>/` and stay immutable as raw input.
- Public website files must be copied into `assets/<case-id>/` before linking in `content/cases/<id>.json`.
- Use one canonical slug per case across folders, JSON filename and `id` (`kondi-nova`, `green-park-93`).
- Keep naming stable for media sequences: `after-1`, `after-2`, `before-1`, `compare-1`, `plan`.
- Never reference `inbox` paths from UI code or from content JSON.
- `js/data.js`, `js/config.js`, `cases/<slug>/index.html` and `sitemap.xml` are AUTO-GENERATED by `scripts/build-pages.py`; never edit them by hand.

## Responsive Image Variants

- `scripts/process-assets.py` stores a 1440px master (JPEG/PNG) and auto-generates derived variants next to it: `<stem>-640.<ext>`, `<stem>-1024.<ext>` (when the master is wider) plus WebP twins (`<stem>.webp`, `<stem>-640.webp`, `<stem>-1024.webp`).
- Reference only master files (`after-1.jpg`, `plan.png`) in content JSON; the build wires srcset/`<picture>` automatically.
- Never hand-edit or hand-create `-640`/`-1024`/`.webp` variant files; regenerate with `python scripts/process-assets.py --optimize-all`.

## Case Onboarding Steps

- Scaffold: `python scripts/scaffold-case.py --title "..."` (creates `content/cases/<id>.json`).
- Import inbox photos with `python scripts/process-assets.py --case <id> --from inbox/<slug>/...` (web resize + compress + variants).
- Or optimize files already in `assets/<case-id>/` with `python scripts/process-assets.py --case <id>`.
- Fill `cover`, `gallery`, `plan` paths in `content/cases/<id>.json` from `assets/<case-id>/...` and verify the files exist.
- If `hasVideo` is true, provide valid `video.fileUrl` and `video.poster`.
- Keep the CTA object complete and consistent with other cases.
- Rebuild and validate: `python scripts/build-pages.py`, then `python scripts/validate-cases.py`.
